 "_comment": "Mission «Корона 3. Балтийская вода, 1433» (mission card in the missions doc, docs/03-missions/14-crown_03_baltic_water_1433.md). A march without a base along one long map, map_crown_03 (tools/maps/gen_crown_03.py), from the siege camp before Chojnice in the south to the shore at Oliwa in the north: four camps with a wagenburg each, Pelplin, Tczew with its wooden suburb, the Bishop's hill above Gdańsk. Player 1 is Jaśko of Łęczyca and his banners with twelve wagons; allies (setup.sides) 3 Mikołaj of Michałów and the Crown's horse, 4 the Czech orphans of Jan Čapek; enemies 2 the Order (Chojnice, Tczew, the raiders) and 5 Gdańsk. Rules in core/mission/mission_baltic.gd (rules.baltic): the concord, the orphans following their leaders, the camps, the wind at Tczew, the garrison giving itself up, the prisoners, the villages, the chapels, hunger and the knighting; the townsmen's sorties are the waves of MissionRetreat. Read by core/mission/mission_def.gd; cells are map cells, ticks 1/20 s, texts are English keys translated through i18n/*.po.",
