 "briefing": {
  "place": "Gdańsk Pomerania, from Chojnice to the sea at Oliwa. Mid-August – 4 September 1433.",
  "story": "King Władysław Jagiełło has hired the Czech «orphans» of Jan Čapek against the Order. Six weeks before Chojnice have brought nothing but three failed assaults. Mikołaj of Michałów, the Crown's commander, has had enough: the army goes north, where the walls are lower. Jaśko of Łęczyca, about forty-five years old, leads his banners and the wagons of the train beside an ally who cannot be trusted in everything.",
  "goal": "Bring the train out of Chojnice, draw up a wagenburg at every camp, take Tczew with fire carried by the wind, bring its prisoners to Mikołaj before the orphans reach them, and come to the sea at Oliwa.",
  "lose": ["Jaśko or Mikołaj of Michałów falls", "More than half of the wagons are lost", "The concord with the orphans breaks down twice"]
 },
