     "do": "cutscene",
     "id": "six_weeks",
     "at": [50, 200],
     "lines": [
      ["Chronicler", "Chojnice, the middle of August 1433. The trenches before the wall, the patched breaches. The Czech wagons stand in a ring, by the fire the Czechs are singing. The Crown's camp stands apart."],
      [
       "Chronicler",
       "More than twenty years after Grunwald the king hired the Czechs, the very ones who burned churches at home. Pan Jan said that his great-grandfather Jaśko, grey already, went with them to the sea and to his death could not decide what there was more of in that march: glory or shame."
      ],
      ["Chronicler", "Čapek rides out of the Czech wagon fort with two horsemen and goes calmly to the town gate. The gate opens a crack."],
      ["hero_mikolaj_michalow", "He is off again. Six weeks we have beaten our heads against this wall, and he goes visiting the commander."],
      ["hero_jasko", "Perhaps he is bargaining for the town."],
      ["hero_mikolaj_michalow", "Perhaps for himself. Enough. Gather the wagons, pan Jaśko. We go north, where the walls are lower."]
     ]
    },
    {"do": "objective", "id": "leave", "text": "Lift the siege of Chojnice and bring the wagons out without loss"},
    {"do": "objective", "id": "monks", "text": "Lead the monks of Pelplin out before the fire", "optional": true},
    {"do": "objective", "id": "chapels", "text": "Set up chapels on all 3 places of power and let the orphans break none", "optional": true},
    {"do": "objective", "id": "concord_half", "text": "Do not let the concord fall below half", "optional": true},
    {"do": "objective", "id": "knights", "text": "Have 3 of Jaśko's banners knighted on the shore", "optional": true},
    {
     "do": "hint",
     "text": "Your twelve wagons carry the army's food. Lead them north out of the trenches, to the road by the first camp. Lose more than half of them and the march is over."
